# Impeccable Craft Rules

This file defines how UI should be implemented at a detailed level.

Craft is about precision, consistency, and subtle polish.

## Core Principle

Do not just make things “look good”.
Make them feel refined, balanced, and intentional.

---

## Attention to Detail

- Spacing must be consistent
- Elements must align visually
- Avoid random values
- Use spacing scale: 4, 6, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32

---

## Consistency

- Reuse the same patterns across components
- Cards must share:
  - same border radius
  - same shadow style
  - same spacing structure
- Do not mix styles arbitrarily

---

## Restraint

- Avoid over-design
- Do not stack too many effects:
  - gradients
  - blur
  - heavy shadows
  - multiple animations
- Keep UI calm and minimal

---

## Polish

- Use smooth transitions:
  - `transition-all duration-300 ease-out`
- Use subtle hover:
  - `hover:-translate-y-1`
  - `hover:shadow-lg`
- Interactions should feel soft, not aggressive

---

## Spacing System

- Use consistent spacing scale:
  - 4, 6, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32
- Avoid arbitrary values
- Ensure enough breathing space between sections

---

## Typography Hierarchy

- Title:
  - `font-semibold`
  - `text-slate-900`
- Body:
  - `text-slate-600`
- Meta:
  - `text-slate-500`
- Keep text easy to scan

---

## Image Quality

- Use `object-cover`
- Maintain consistent aspect ratio
- Avoid broken images
- Images must feel high-quality and relevant

---

## Motion

- Use subtle animation only
- Avoid flashy or distracting motion
- Motion should enhance clarity, not distract

---

## Implementation Constraints

- Do not change logic
- Do not change routes
- Keep code simple and readable
- Prefer Tailwind utilities
- Maintain consistency across all components

---

## Goal

The UI should feel:

- clean
- premium
- calm
- intentional
- well-crafted
